WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.272 --> 00:00:01.654
- I'm just excited for a new outfit.

00:00:01.654 --> 00:00:05.113
I really, really enjoy
people reinterpreting

00:00:05.113 --> 00:00:07.202
who I am, if that makes sense.

00:00:07.202 --> 00:00:08.921
(sign creaks)

00:00:08.921 --> 00:00:13.433
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.463 --> 00:00:18.224
- Fashion, for me, is something
I take a lot of pride in.

00:00:18.224 --> 00:00:20.174
- I dress more sharply,

00:00:20.174 --> 00:00:21.876
and so I would like to break out of that.

00:00:21.876 --> 00:00:25.643
- I roll out of bed like 30
minutes before I start work.

00:00:25.643 --> 00:00:27.082
- I can picture Nick in my mind,

00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:28.986
and I can picture clothes he's worn,

00:00:28.986 --> 00:00:30.960
but I don't know if I ever had an opinion

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.167
about stuff he's wearing.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:33.687
- [Nick] I, you know,
I put myself together,

00:00:33.687 --> 00:00:34.866
and it looks halfway decent.

00:00:34.866 --> 00:00:38.709
- I want to find a fun, patterned,

00:00:38.709 --> 00:00:42.064
collared shirt, more like '80s and '90s.

00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:43.550
- I think her wardrobe
is just a little bit

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.406
more daring and abrasive than mine is,

00:00:46.406 --> 00:00:47.868
and I really like that, though.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:51.143
- I mean, I have no idea what
that girl is gonna put me in.

00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:52.663
- This is how much I know about fashion.

00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:55.206
I'm like, I'll put Nick
in a shirt and pants.

00:00:55.206 --> 00:00:56.668
Oh, it's gonna be great.

00:00:56.668 --> 00:01:00.627
I straight up have never shopped
for a guy in my life, ever.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.823
So we'll see.

00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:03.873
I didn't know where to start,
there's so many options here

00:01:03.873 --> 00:01:07.379
that when you first are sent
out, it's very very scary.

00:01:07.379 --> 00:01:10.221
I had a couple of mini panic attacks.

00:01:10.221 --> 00:01:11.474
These are pretty cute.

00:01:11.474 --> 00:01:12.914
- Even though I don't dress the same way

00:01:12.914 --> 00:01:15.263
as, say, Jazzmyne does, I can tell

00:01:15.263 --> 00:01:17.654
that she has an eye for color and style.

00:01:17.654 --> 00:01:22.610
- I was going for a street
vibe meets a Zack Morris vibe.

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.673
I really want squooshy pants.

00:01:24.673 --> 00:01:27.348
Or should I have him
looking like Missy Elliott?

00:01:27.348 --> 00:01:29.579
- I feel like I only notice clothes

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:32.643
if they are super flashy or are

00:01:32.643 --> 00:01:35.973
obviously meant to be silly or bad.

00:01:35.973 --> 00:01:37.027
Tiger's our intern.

00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:39.330
Tiger, do you think this looks cool?

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.633
Would you wear it? Be honest.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:44.354
- I'm not asking you any
more questions, Tiger.

00:01:44.354 --> 00:01:46.594
You're clearly out to sabotage me.

00:01:46.594 --> 00:01:49.376
- In order to be street-styled correctly,

00:01:49.376 --> 00:01:51.310
you need a dope jacket.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.343
Wow!

00:01:52.343 --> 00:01:55.315
- I think if I went with
this jacket and this blue,

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:57.080
I think this actually looks really nice.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.127
- [Voiceover] Don't fuck it up.

00:01:58.127 --> 00:01:59.714
- I will, probably.

00:01:59.714 --> 00:02:01.769
- I just hope it looks halfway decent.

00:02:01.769 --> 00:02:03.405
- This is the thing, I don't
know how to shop for myself,

00:02:03.405 --> 00:02:05.043
I certainly don't know
how to shop for a man.

00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:06.238
- I'm excited I get to do this.

00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:08.665
I used to walk around stores
and put outfits together,

00:02:08.665 --> 00:02:10.289
and hope someone would pick them up.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:12.263
I kind of don't mind shirts like these,

00:02:12.263 --> 00:02:13.564
'cause they're so wrong.

00:02:13.564 --> 00:02:14.910
- I guess what makes me
feel insecure about it

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.297
is that I feel like if I do a bad job,

00:02:16.297 --> 00:02:17.911
everyone will make fun of me.

00:02:17.911 --> 00:02:19.593
I just need to do something big.

00:02:21.595 --> 00:02:23.789
- [Jazzmyne] 'Cause this
kind of matches with these.

00:02:23.789 --> 00:02:26.784
- I think this is a perfect
shoe to go with this outfit

00:02:26.784 --> 00:02:30.244
because the outfit in itself
is a little bit darker colored,

00:02:30.244 --> 00:02:31.718
not super flashy.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.225
I think this adds just
the right amount of glam.

00:02:34.225 --> 00:02:37.198
And I think Nick is ready to
go out and solve a mystery,

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:39.925
a murder mystery, in the outfit I got him.

00:02:39.925 --> 00:02:41.423
- I'm excited for it, I'd wear it.

00:02:41.423 --> 00:02:42.619
- We're gonna go back to the office

00:02:42.619 --> 00:02:44.026
and try all our stuff on.

00:02:44.026 --> 00:02:48.590
(electric guitar)

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.682
(Nick and Jen laugh)

00:02:49.682 --> 00:02:50.743
- [Jen] You can't pose like that.

00:02:50.743 --> 00:02:54.064
- What the (bleep) is this?

00:02:54.064 --> 00:02:56.030
It's some damn clown shoes.

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.630
(Jazzmyne laughs)

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.417
- Is this what you wanted?

00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:01.811
- Not completely.

00:03:01.811 --> 00:03:03.030
Tie this around your waist.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.794
- Oh, now I get it.

00:03:04.794 --> 00:03:07.139
- Oh my gosh, look at him!

00:03:07.139 --> 00:03:11.052
- If I was a straight woman or a gay man,

00:03:11.052 --> 00:03:14.175
I'd be like, wassup?

00:03:14.175 --> 00:03:15.997
Look at all those patterns!

00:03:15.997 --> 00:03:17.803
- I'm like a fashionable background extra

00:03:17.803 --> 00:03:18.929
for Saved by the Bell.

00:03:18.929 --> 00:03:20.125
- There we go.

00:03:20.125 --> 00:03:21.437
- I never thought that I would be able

00:03:21.437 --> 00:03:22.783
to pull off thrift-store chic.

00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:25.081
- I'm really, really
happy with what I got.

00:03:25.081 --> 00:03:28.925
And I also feel like he's
always very put together,

00:03:28.925 --> 00:03:31.246
and I think this will help
him step out of his style,

00:03:31.246 --> 00:03:34.822
into a style that's a
little bit more carefree

00:03:34.822 --> 00:03:36.203
and just like, whatever.

00:03:36.203 --> 00:03:38.107
- I'm just hoping that the great outfit

00:03:38.107 --> 00:03:40.730
that she picked for me will inspire me

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.368
to continue dressing like that

00:03:42.368 --> 00:03:43.969
and going off of that more.

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:46.048
- That (bleep) was a damn mess.

00:03:46.048 --> 00:03:47.882
I mean, a trench coat, really?

00:03:47.882 --> 00:03:49.542
Who wears trench coats?

00:03:49.542 --> 00:03:53.431
Who wears polka dots with
other sorts of patterns?

00:03:53.431 --> 00:03:54.720
I just, I can't.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.588
- I guess it wasn't up to his style,

00:03:56.588 --> 00:03:57.703
and I wouldn't wanna force somebody

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.793
to wear something they don't like.

00:03:59.793 --> 00:04:03.385
So I will be okay if Nick
doesn't wear the outfit again.

00:04:03.385 --> 00:04:07.712
(rock music)

00:04:08.752 --> 00:04:10.661
(sign creaks)

